From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ai_re <ai_re@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] board: alpine-v2: hand the al_eth board params and MAC to
 Linux

The vendor al_eth driver (Linux, and the vendor U-Boot's own) reads the
integrated Ethernet port's wiring from three scratch registers in the MAC
BAR ("board params": MAC +0x4, +0x404, +0xc) and its MAC address from
forwarding MAC entry 0 in the EC BAR (+0x868/+0x86c). Without the params
probe fails ("board info not available"); without the MAC it picks a
random one. The vendor U-Boot leaves both behind after a network command;
a boot path that never ran one gave Linux neither.

Right before Linux is entered (board_prep_linux), for every PCI 1c36:0001
function:
- params already present are kept (the firmware is authoritative; a
  mismatch with the DT is only reported); missing ones are encoded from
  the function's DT node (phy-mode rgmii*/sgmii + fixed-link, no MDIO
  PHY) exactly as the HAL's al_eth_board_params_set() would;
- the MAC is env ethaddr (eth<N>addr) if set, else what the EC already
  holds, else the ONIE TlvInfo EEPROM named by "amazon,mac-eeprom"
  (TLV 0x24, CRC-32 checked);
- what it found and did is printed; failures say what Linux will do.

include/alpine_v2_eth.h holds the offsets and the pure encoders/parsers,
so a host test can check them against the HAL (al_hal_eth_main.c) and
its register structs. "aleth info" shows the state read-only, "aleth
handoff" runs the handoff now.

Scope: alpine-v2.
---
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/Kconfig       |  20 ++
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/MAINTAINERS   |   1 +
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/Makefile      |   1 +
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/eth-handoff.c | 385 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/alpine_v2_eth.h              | 175 ++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 582 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 board/amazon/alpine-v2/eth-handoff.c
 create mode 100644 include/alpine_v2_eth.h

